// REAL RESPONSE EXAMPLE — GET /api/v1/telemetry (computed live, not served from this file)
// Captured from the dev machine on 2026-08-05. Values change on every request.
// Variability notes:
//   - uptime_seconds        : host boot uptime (time.time() - psutil.boot_time())
//   - cpu.per_core_percent  : one entry per logical CPU core (length = core count)
//   - gpu                   : one entry per GPU; NVIDIA and AMD can coexist;
//                             empty array [] when no supported GPU is present
//   - gpu[].vendor          : "NVIDIA" (pynvml) or "AMD" (amdsmi)
//   - power_sensors         : one entry per hwmon device with available sensors;
//                             reads voltage (V), current (A), power (W), temperature (°C)
//                             from /sys/class/hwmon; empty array [] when no sensors found
//   - power_supply          : one entry per battery from /sys/class/power_supply;
//                             provides battery-specific metrics (voltage, energy, capacity,
//                             status, cycle count, manufacturer); empty array [] when no batteries
